WEBVTT

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>tsukinuketa aoi sora</b>

00:00:15.390 --> 00:00:19.040
<b>The blue sky has broken through</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>saa dekakeyou</b>

00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:22.040
<b>Come, let's go out</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>itsumo no namikimichi jitensha wo koideku</b>

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:28.880
<b>Riding my bike through the usual avenue</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>ima sugu ni aitai yo</b>

00:00:29.630 --> 00:00:33.550
<b>"I want to meet you now."</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>omoi ga kaze wo kiri</b>

00:00:33.550 --> 00:00:37.100
<b>That thought is blown away by the wind,</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>kimi e to hakondeku tegami ni natte</b>

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:44.770
<b>and becomes a letter being carried to you</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>koko kara hajimaru monogatari fly!</b>

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:52.360
<b>The story that starts from here... Fly!</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.620
<b>kawariyuku kisetsu ga ashioto wo tatetemo</b>

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:59.620
<b>Even if the changing seasons walk on with loud footsteps,</b>

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>sou kawaranai suki to iu tsubasa</b>

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:06.500
<b>the wings of love won't change</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>dokomade mo tondeke oozora takaku</b>

00:01:07.130 --> 00:01:14.510
<b>Fly far away, high into the sky</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.680
<b>koi no tenki yohou hare nochi hare ni nare</b>

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:20.680
<b>May the weather forecast of love be sunny and clear forever</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.350
<b>ashita mo asatte mo</b>

00:01:21.640 --> 00:01:28.350
<b>Tomorrow and the day after tomorrow</b>

00:01:30.020 --> 00:01:34.940
<b>Episode 14    Dream-Colored Message</b>

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:54.420
Mom!

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.030
Mom!

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:02.430
What time is it?

00:02:03.510 --> 00:02:05.430
Are you there?

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.600
Shou-chan!

00:02:33.380 --> 00:02:34.210
It's Tama!

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:36.060
Good morning.

00:02:36.060 --> 00:02:39.680
<i>Not good morning, it's already 10 o'clock!</i>

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.140
10 o'clock?

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:45.390
I missed the first sunrise of the year again—

00:02:45.390 --> 00:02:48.410
<i>The first sunrise of the year was three days ago!</i>

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:50.100
<i>It's the 4th today.</i>

00:02:50.730 --> 00:02:58.150
But I've been working at Raifuku Shrine 
from New Year's Eve until yesterday.

00:02:58.650 --> 00:03:03.910
And I thought I could relax and 
watch TV during New Year's—

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.330
There were so many people 
doing New Year's shrine visits.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:13.130
I had no idea shrines were this busy at New Year's.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:17.840
This is no laughing matter.

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.510
I bet you were only lying under the kotatsu all the time.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.100
You haven't visited a single time.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:26.030
I'm sorry.

00:03:26.030 --> 00:03:29.350
As a poverty god, it's a little hard for me to go there.

00:03:30.810 --> 00:03:31.740
Bin-chan?

00:03:31.740 --> 00:03:33.940
Did Tama withdraw herself?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.730
Yes.

00:03:36.230 --> 00:03:37.520
I see.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:40.530
Anyway, Happy New Year.

00:03:41.240 --> 00:03:43.110
Happy New Year.

00:03:43.110 --> 00:03:46.240
I'm still the poverty god, but here's to another year.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:56.000
Where is everyone?

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.260
Your father and mother had 
breakfast and went to visit a grave.

00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:04.300
Shoukichi-san is in his room.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:07.930
I see.

00:04:15.100 --> 00:04:18.150
Bin-chan, could you bring me some breakfast?

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:20.860
Me?

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:25.070
I don't want to get out of the kotatsu.

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:29.830
I'm still tired from the past few days.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:31.870
I understand.

00:04:33.290 --> 00:04:34.970
<i>How rude!</i>

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.540
<i>Yurie-chan's the one that's only 
lying under the kotatsu all day!</i>

00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:39.750
Oh well—

00:04:41.260 --> 00:04:42.920
Thanks for the food!

00:04:44.760 --> 00:04:46.720
<i>There's still some left.</i>

00:04:48.260 --> 00:04:51.680
I don't like black soy beans.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:54.230
<i>Well, neither do I, but—</i>

00:04:54.730 --> 00:04:57.480
<i>If you don't eat up your 
breakfast, you'll be punished for it.</i>

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.860
<i>Did you know there are 7 
gods in a single grain of rice?</i>

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:10.080
That'd be cannibalism.

00:05:10.410 --> 00:05:12.250
Besides, it's just superstition.

00:05:15.710 --> 00:05:19.380
There's nothing interesting on TV—

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:27.760
New Year's Debut Singers: Chanson Show.

00:05:29.100 --> 00:05:33.640
A pro baseball match, sumo 
wrestling, a national singing contest—

00:05:34.850 --> 00:05:37.650
The First Laugh: Hilarity Parade.

00:05:53.490 --> 00:05:55.750
What the hell are you doing?

00:06:01.340 --> 00:06:04.260
Tama, don't snatch away food!

00:06:33.740 --> 00:06:34.620
My—

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:37.620
Looks like we'll have a handful 
with Tama this year as well!

00:06:40.960 --> 00:06:43.590
Whatever, I don't care anymore.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:51.970
Didn't you go visit the grave, Shou-chan?

00:06:53.300 --> 00:06:54.560
I'll go later.

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:57.560
I'm going to visit the shrine with some friends today.

00:06:58.060 --> 00:06:58.860
Why now?

00:06:58.860 --> 00:07:02.980
I was at Raifuku Shrine until yesterday.

00:07:03.310 --> 00:07:04.570
That's exactly why.

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:08.400
Why should I have to visit god Yurie on New Year's?

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:18.040
By the way, Miko-chan has—

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.090
Bring me a pen.

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.620
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hHilarity! Comedy 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hTheater "Glasses 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hParadise", or 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h"glas-a-dise" 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hfor short. Long 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hstory Mega 
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hand Megane's 
\h\h\h\h\hMega-hide. 
\h\hKuratatei 
Eyeglasses

00:07:53.700 --> 00:07:56.620
\h\h\h\h\h\h\hIt's New Year's! 
\h\h\h\h\h\hGathering of 
\h\h\h\h\hkids. Kimono's 
\h\h\hand splashes? 
\h\hSuzuki Riko 
[N] News flash

00:07:55.410 --> 00:07:56.240
So—

00:07:58.370 --> 00:08:00.540
What was up with Saegusa?

00:08:02.750 --> 00:08:05.380
She told me to hand you a fortune strip she gave me.

00:08:05.380 --> 00:08:06.670
A fortune strip?

00:08:07.500 --> 00:08:10.720
As an apology for causing you trouble last year.

00:08:12.800 --> 00:08:17.560
Aren't those kind of pointless 
unless you draw them yourself?

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:20.430
But you never came.

00:08:20.430 --> 00:08:24.270
It's a New Year's limited edition deluxe fortune strip.

00:08:28.230 --> 00:08:30.070
So where is it?

00:08:32.070 --> 00:08:33.900
I left it in my pocket.

00:08:34.360 --> 00:08:35.360
Where are your clothes?

00:08:36.070 --> 00:08:38.510
When I took a bath yesterday,

00:08:38.510 --> 00:08:40.330
I put them in the basket—

00:08:41.830 --> 00:08:44.170
Mom probably put them in the laundry!

00:08:47.380 --> 00:08:49.500
How could you do something so unthoughtful!?

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:52.670
Shou-chan, turn on the TV!

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:54.550
Do it yourself.

00:08:56.640 --> 00:08:57.930
The TV—

00:09:39.640 --> 00:09:42.430
<i>—and here are the holes in which the candy is hidden.</i>

00:09:42.430 --> 00:09:45.020
<i>However, you are not allowed to use your hands.</i>

00:09:43.890 --> 00:09:44.770
I did it!

00:09:45.020 --> 00:09:47.520
<i>Please look for the candy using just your face!</i>

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.440
It's on the wrong channel—

00:09:47.520 --> 00:09:49.440
<i>But this is too easy, isn't it?</i>

00:09:49.440 --> 00:09:53.610
<i>Indeed! Mixed inside the candy is another, special wasabi candy.</i>

00:09:51.770 --> 00:09:55.950
I want a TV with a remote control—

00:09:53.610 --> 00:09:56.200
<i>How will it taste when put in your mouth?</i>

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:58.410
<i>It'll be something that surprises even sushi makers!</i>

00:09:58.410 --> 00:10:00.990
<i>You can already feel it won't be something good!</i>

00:10:00.990 --> 00:10:03.580
<i>The grand prize is 10 million yen, after all!</i>

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:06.370
Kamichu!

00:10:07.870 --> 00:10:13.130
<i>—and then we saw something incredible flying in the eastern sky!</i>

00:10:13.630 --> 00:10:17.680
<i>It was— a giant hammer!</i>

00:10:18.130 --> 00:10:22.050
<i>With the handle up front, it shot up like a rocket!</i>

00:10:22.050 --> 00:10:24.470
<i>We couldn't believe our eyes!</i>

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:27.940
<i>A hammer is something you hit nails with, not something that flies through the eastern sky!</i>

00:10:27.940 --> 00:10:31.360
<i>What do you think of that, researcher of paranormal phenomena, Hadayama-sensei!?</i>

00:10:31.360 --> 00:10:32.820
<i>It was an optical illusion.</i>

00:10:33.520 --> 00:10:36.490
<i>There were many eye-witnesses besides us, you know!</i>

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:43.490
<i>It is predicted that congestions due to people returning from home will peak this evening.</i>

00:10:43.490 --> 00:10:50.580
<i>Operating bullet trains are exceeding 100 percent capacity, filled with sight of exhausted families.</i>

00:10:49.420 --> 00:10:53.670
Yuri-chan, don't leave the TV on.

00:10:55.420 --> 00:10:58.880
Dad, don't take pictures of me like this!

00:10:59.260 --> 00:11:00.720
What are you saying?

00:11:00.720 --> 00:11:03.850
These will become precious records 
of my cute daughter growing up.

00:11:05.260 --> 00:11:08.850
Then at least take pictures of 
parts where I'm actually growing.

00:11:08.850 --> 00:11:11.560
"A child that sleeps well grows up 
strong" is what they say, don't they?

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:14.110
That's right.

00:11:14.110 --> 00:11:19.500
It'd be nice if you could grow 
for another 30 centimeters or so.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:21.030
That's too tall!

00:11:21.820 --> 00:11:26.080
We already cleaned the grave, 
so you should visit as well.

00:11:26.540 --> 00:11:28.040
Yes—

00:11:28.040 --> 00:11:31.790
You haven't visited since you became a god, have you?

00:11:31.790 --> 00:11:34.380
I'm sure grandpa will be surprised!

00:11:34.380 --> 00:11:35.470
Yeah.

00:11:35.470 --> 00:11:38.550
He might come back to life from shock!

00:11:38.550 --> 00:11:39.510
Right?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:42.640
Coming!

00:11:45.010 --> 00:11:46.810
Hello, Hitotsubashi household.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:51.100
Have you been sleeping all day until now?

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:52.380
A Happy New Year to you too!

00:11:52.380 --> 00:11:54.690
Please stay friends with Yuri-chan this year as well!

00:11:55.110 --> 00:11:56.820
It's Mitsue-chan.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.530
Coming!

00:12:01.900 --> 00:12:02.860
What are you doing?

00:12:05.450 --> 00:12:06.740
It's cold out there.

00:12:11.250 --> 00:12:13.330
Such bad manners.

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.380
I've been sleeping all day.

00:12:20.880 --> 00:12:24.640
Because, I've been working for days.

00:12:27.050 --> 00:12:28.250
I guess you did.

00:12:28.250 --> 00:12:31.140
So, wanna go to Izumi tomorrow?

00:12:31.140 --> 00:12:33.480
They're still having their New Year's sale.

00:12:33.980 --> 00:12:36.730
We received our New Year's presents, 
so you have some money to spend, right?

00:12:37.690 --> 00:12:38.770
New Year's present?

00:12:40.990 --> 00:12:43.150
Okay! I'll go with you!

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.870
Then, I'll call you again tomorrow.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.870
Okay, see you later.

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.250
Dad!

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:01.630
I haven't received my New Year's present yet!

00:13:01.630 --> 00:13:04.510
Well, you see, it's already the 4th.

00:13:04.510 --> 00:13:06.510
The time period for a New Year's present has passed—

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:10.640
No way! If you cheat me, I'll curse you!

00:13:11.850 --> 00:13:13.480
Okay, okay!

00:13:13.480 --> 00:13:15.520
I'll give it, I'll give it!

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.600
I did it!

00:13:19.570 --> 00:13:22.570
You've grown more than I thought.

00:13:23.610 --> 00:13:24.780
Your weight, I mean.

00:13:25.110 --> 00:13:26.660
How mean!

00:13:26.660 --> 00:13:29.530
Yuri-chan, did you eat the black soy beans?

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:34.660
I put them aside because I 
seasoned them with red peppers—

00:13:39.500 --> 00:13:42.420
We're going to see grandma.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.930
We'll be back for dinner, so don't steal any food!

00:13:48.930 --> 00:13:50.600
And put some clothes on,

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:53.270
it's indecent to stay like that!

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:54.970
Okay!

00:13:59.150 --> 00:14:00.360
Oh, my—

00:14:03.320 --> 00:14:04.230
Yuri-chan?

00:14:06.570 --> 00:14:09.110
Here are your New Year's cards for today.

00:14:14.910 --> 00:14:18.250
I left the cards from the past few days under the TV.

00:14:19.460 --> 00:14:21.090
Why there?

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:22.280
Bye!

00:14:22.280 --> 00:14:24.000
We're off!

00:14:39.190 --> 00:14:41.940
<i>I hate black soy beans!</i>

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.440
If you're picky with food, you won't grow up well.

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.700
<i>I don't want to hear that coming from you.</i>

00:14:50.740 --> 00:14:52.700
<i>You received so many.</i>

00:14:55.950 --> 00:15:01.880
<i>From your friends, the Prime Minister, 
the martian and battleship Yamato—</i>

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:05.800
<i>That's quite a line-up.</i>

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:09.630
It's not here—

00:15:19.690 --> 00:15:23.190
About tomorrow, I'll be at the train station at 10 o'clock.

00:15:23.190 --> 00:15:25.190
Let's meet at the ticket gate.

00:15:25.770 --> 00:15:26.400
Okay.

00:15:27.780 --> 00:15:29.780
Hey, Matsuri-chan—

00:15:29.780 --> 00:15:30.860
What is it?

00:15:35.410 --> 00:15:39.040
Did you get a New Year's card from Ninomiya-kun?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:40.210
I did.

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:43.920
I have no idea what it says though.

00:15:43.920 --> 00:15:46.130
Mitsue said the same thing.

00:15:48.510 --> 00:15:50.920
Even Mitsue-chan got one—

00:15:52.550 --> 00:15:54.550
You didn't get one?

00:15:56.680 --> 00:15:58.970
It's— probably just a little late!

00:15:59.310 --> 00:16:02.390
You know Ken-chan makes mistakes like that!

00:16:02.980 --> 00:16:05.610
He was busy working on New Year's as well!

00:16:07.480 --> 00:16:08.480
Thanks.

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:12.910
It might have gotten lost by accident at the postal service.

00:16:13.530 --> 00:16:18.370
Delivery of New Year's greetings 
is likely done by part-timers.

00:16:18.870 --> 00:16:21.000
There might have been a mistake—

00:16:22.410 --> 00:16:23.320
Thanks.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:26.210
You're kind, Bin-chan.

00:16:26.210 --> 00:16:28.340
Err— I—

00:16:30.210 --> 00:16:31.260
I understand.

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:33.260
Even if I don't get a New Year's card,

00:16:33.260 --> 00:16:35.930
he can still greet me at school.

00:16:36.850 --> 00:16:40.680
Ninomiya-kun is a very busy person.

00:16:44.650 --> 00:16:47.060
So, I won't feel sad.

00:16:47.480 --> 00:16:51.070
It's time to open up my New Year's present!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:53.400
Your New Year's present?

00:16:56.200 --> 00:16:57.660
I'm already a second year middle school student.

00:16:57.660 --> 00:16:59.030
It's okay to expect something nice.

00:17:03.000 --> 00:17:04.040
5000 yen!

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:08.090
It's a new record!

00:17:09.000 --> 00:17:12.590
You normally only see something like this at New Year's!

00:17:13.420 --> 00:17:16.180
Well, it is New Year's—

00:17:16.970 --> 00:17:18.760
But this is—

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:21.310
You've never seen a 5000 yen bill before?

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.480
I'm the poverty god.

00:17:25.020 --> 00:17:29.150
I've never had anything beyond a 1000 yen bill.

00:17:30.770 --> 00:17:34.780
You can buy 50 glasses of juice 
with only one of these bills!

00:17:35.820 --> 00:17:38.660
Wow, that's amazing—

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:41.370
Sign: 1000 yen

00:17:45.290 --> 00:17:46.870
Why!?

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.340
I'm sorry.

00:17:49.340 --> 00:17:53.340
My poverty god's instinct suddenly took over—

00:18:02.260 --> 00:18:03.350
I'm home.

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:31.420
Are you still sleeping!?

00:18:32.670 --> 00:18:33.450
Yeah.

00:18:34.000 --> 00:18:37.470
Did you visit the shrine?

00:18:37.880 --> 00:18:39.470
That's what I told you, didn't I?

00:18:52.270 --> 00:18:54.650
Did you find the fortune strip?

00:18:56.610 --> 00:18:59.200
I didn't, so I went to draw one myself.

00:18:59.910 --> 00:19:02.410
You have to draw a fortune strip yourself, after all.

00:19:03.780 --> 00:19:05.240
So, what was it?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.170
Shoukichi-kun got shoukichi?

00:19:14.960 --> 00:19:17.170
Note: shoukichi = a little luck

00:19:17.170 --> 00:19:20.260
Don't say the same thing as Saegusa.

00:19:20.590 --> 00:19:22.550
Did Miko-chan say that as well?

00:19:25.220 --> 00:19:25.870
Yeah.

00:19:26.280 --> 00:19:29.850
She was making fun of how it matched so well.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:31.130
I see.

00:19:31.420 --> 00:19:35.650
Fortune strips during New Year's are 
generally fixed to "great luck" anyway.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:38.320
I didn't need to know that.

00:19:35.650 --> 00:19:41.610
Love relationship: 
Patience will be rewarded

00:19:39.150 --> 00:19:41.610
I'm satisfied with this.

00:19:43.910 --> 00:19:46.120
There was another New Year's card in the mail.

00:19:49.080 --> 00:19:53.500
The writing is atrocious, so the post 
office probably made a mistake.

00:19:53.500 --> 00:19:55.130
It was redelivered here.

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.510
Hitotsubashi Yurie

00:19:58.090 --> 00:20:00.510
Ninomiya Kenji

00:20:03.390 --> 00:20:05.260
What's written there?

00:20:06.260 --> 00:20:08.010
It says, "Happy New Year.

00:20:08.010 --> 00:20:12.980
Let's do our best to stay good friends this year."

00:20:15.020 --> 00:20:17.650
No, that much wasn't written on there—

00:20:18.150 --> 00:20:19.820
Thanks, Shou-chan!

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.610
I'm sure great things will happen to you this year!

00:20:23.610 --> 00:20:25.280
What's up with you all of a sudden?

00:20:25.740 --> 00:20:28.580
To show my appreciation, I'll give you something good!

00:20:29.700 --> 00:20:33.170
Ultra luck

00:20:33.670 --> 00:20:34.710
Hey!

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.590
Ultra luck

00:20:36.130 --> 00:20:39.590
Love relationship: 
On-and-off sexiness hell

00:20:37.130 --> 00:20:39.590
What kind of worthless stuff is this?

00:20:39.590 --> 00:20:41.770
Don't use strange powers!

00:20:41.770 --> 00:20:43.340
I was fine with how it was!

00:20:43.340 --> 00:20:45.090
Return it back to normal!

00:20:45.890 --> 00:20:47.470
You can have it!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:50.350
It's a New Year's present from your big sister!

00:20:50.350 --> 00:20:53.290
That's not the point! Return it—

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:53.290
We're home!

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:55.310
We're back!

00:20:56.810 --> 00:20:59.190
We finally have our family together.

00:20:59.190 --> 00:21:02.780
Kenkichi-san, Tama-chan isn't here, is she?

00:21:02.780 --> 00:21:04.030
Oh, yeah.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:06.490
Tama is part of the family as well, of course.

00:21:07.870 --> 00:21:11.840
So that means we'll have to give 
Tama a New Year's present as well.

00:21:11.840 --> 00:21:15.000
Wanna go crazy and give her 1500 yen?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.250
"A coin to a cat" is what they say, right?

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:17.250
Note: neko ni koban - to cast pearls before swine

00:21:18.540 --> 00:21:20.590
You're not making sense, Akane-san.

00:21:21.380 --> 00:21:25.380
1500 yen? That's more than me—

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:28.050
Anyway, give me back my fortune strip!

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:29.530
By the way,

00:21:29.530 --> 00:21:34.020
Yuri-chan, there was a fortune strip 
in your pocket, so I took it out.

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:37.020
Where did you leave it!?

00:21:37.770 --> 00:21:41.530
I'm pretty sure I put it in the freezer—

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:45.150
Why in there?

00:21:45.150 --> 00:21:46.780
Because it brings luck.

00:21:56.830 --> 00:21:58.920
Sign: Great curse - Love relationship: A fruitless effort! - Finances: Beware of cats!

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:04.840
Ultra luck

00:22:02.750 --> 00:22:04.840
Great curse

00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:21.230
I'm not sure what's going on, but 
this is proof that you're growing up!

00:22:27.610 --> 00:22:30.370
You can do this tomorrow as well, can't you?

00:22:30.990 --> 00:22:31.710
No!

00:22:31.710 --> 00:22:35.120
Ninomiya-kun must be waiting for my reply.

00:22:35.830 --> 00:22:39.460
I have to take this to the post 
office first thing in the morning!

00:22:40.880 --> 00:22:42.880
I wonder if he really is waiting—

00:22:43.630 --> 00:22:44.350
That's right.

00:22:44.350 --> 00:22:47.840
A New Year's card is the very first greeting of the year.

00:22:47.840 --> 00:22:51.640
If you receive one, you have to 
give a proper and prompt reply.

00:22:55.350 --> 00:22:57.480
This year will be a great year!

00:22:58.060 --> 00:23:00.060
That would be nice—

00:23:03.900 --> 00:23:04.730
What was that?

00:23:22.000 --> 00:23:24.710
Happy New Year!

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:27.760
Sorry for fluttering in so late!

00:23:27.760 --> 00:23:30.930
We brought the New Year's 
greetings from the association!

00:23:30.930 --> 00:23:33.800
As expected, Yurie-sama is very popular!

00:23:33.800 --> 00:23:36.010
You received a lot of New Year's cards!

00:23:37.810 --> 00:23:39.080
New Year's cards?

00:23:39.080 --> 00:23:41.190
From the gods?

00:23:41.690 --> 00:23:44.270
Yeah, it was extremely heavy.

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:46.070
It was a pain just to load them all into—

00:23:47.400 --> 00:23:50.110
Please accept them, Yurie-sama.

00:23:50.610 --> 00:23:51.820
One, two—

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:04.040
New Year's cards from the many gods!

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:07.380
Let's do our best together this year as well!

00:24:09.300 --> 00:24:11.800
Are you going to write replies?

00:24:14.340 --> 00:24:17.560
It'll be another busy year.

00:24:24.300 --> 00:24:30.390
<b>mada mada zenzen owannai last ichijikan no jugyou desu</b>

00:24:24.300 --> 00:24:30.390
<b>The last class of the day never seems to end</b>

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:35.300
<b>tokei wo chira chira mitemo ichi byou ga nagai ne</b>

00:24:30.390 --> 00:24:35.300
<b>Even if I keep glancing at my watch, a second seems an eternity</b>

00:24:36.310 --> 00:24:42.350
<b>mabushii koutei mieru kimi no hashiru sugata oikake</b>

00:24:36.310 --> 00:24:42.350
<b>In the radiant schoolyard, trailing your running visage,</b>

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:47.490
<b>houkago love-love date mousou shite bosou chuu</b>

00:24:42.350 --> 00:24:47.490
<b>my imagination is running wild about our date after class</b>

00:24:48.390 --> 00:24:51.410
<b>chime no kane koi no signal</b>

00:24:48.390 --> 00:24:51.410
<b>The school chimes ring and it's a signal of love!</b>

00:24:51.410 --> 00:24:54.380
<b>rouka no tobidashi ni wa chuui</b>

00:24:51.410 --> 00:24:54.380
<b>Be careful if you rush out into the hallway!</b>

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:57.350
<b>kimi no moto e ichiban saki ni</b>

00:24:54.380 --> 00:24:57.350
<b>I dash to see you, first thing!</b>

00:24:57.350 --> 00:24:59.990
<b>issho ni kaerou</b>

00:24:57.350 --> 00:24:59.990
<b>Let's go home together!</b>

00:25:00.970 --> 00:25:07.610
<b>soda aji no ice candy gira gira na ohisama no shita hanbunko</b>

00:25:00.970 --> 00:25:07.610
<b>Sharing a soda-flavored popsicle under the glaring sun</b>

00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:13.650
<b>torokesou na atashi no seishun desu doki doki shichau</b>

00:25:07.610 --> 00:25:13.650
<b>My youth seems to melt with it, it makes my heart beat faster</b>

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:19.140
<b>kono nanigenai toki wo ima mune ni shimatte</b>

00:25:13.650 --> 00:25:19.140
<b>I'm shutting our casual time in my heart</b>

00:25:19.440 --> 00:25:26.560
<b>asu wa mata kyou yori mo kimi wo suki ni naru no desu</b>

00:25:19.440 --> 00:25:26.560
<b>Tomorrow I will love you even more than today</b>

00:25:30.770 --> 00:25:36.680
Valentine's Day is the day when girls muster up 
their courage for a decisive battle of love and cacao!

00:25:30.770 --> 00:25:45.770
<b>Preview</b>

00:25:36.680 --> 00:25:40.510
I will give chocolates to Ninomiya-kun this year.

00:25:40.510 --> 00:25:42.250
Next time, "A Small Step".

00:25:40.680 --> 00:25:45.770
<b>A Small Step</b>

00:25:42.250 --> 00:25:44.890
Let's bring this to a climax together!
